        "date": "2026-11-26T23:04:18Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): one HEIDENHAIN dialect resolver for the DIN/ISO and Klartext posts\n\nThe resolver in camcraft_post::post::heidenhain_dialect maps\ncontroller.identity (model, NC software, installed options) to a profile\nand its capability flags, from docs/research/heidenhain. The engine gives\nit to the scripts as machine.heidenhainDialect. An unknown model, a\nparaxial model, a malformed identifier or a release that the research does\nnot name is refused by name.\n\nThe DIN/ISO post reads languageIso, drillC200 (replaces the #4172 table)\nand cycle247. The Klartext post reads m140, cycle247, m136m137 and\ndecimals. The Picomax output does not change.\n\nRefs #4095\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
